Why is an Adjacency Matrix a suitable choice for a small, fixed number of delivery hubs compared to an Adjacency List?

An adjacency matrix works well because there are only a small number of cities, so it is easy to store and check connections.
It also makes finding the fuel cost between two cities quick. An adjacency list could save more space,
but a matrix is simpler for a small network where the number of cities isn't changing much.
